Lunacy's Software Manager.

Palm's own Software Manager (com.palm.app.swmanager 3.0.3400, webOS 3.x) listed the apps on
a webOS device, deleted them, and offered updates from HP's App Catalog. Lunacy's lists every
app its launcher can show, webOS and Android, and lets the user hide any of them from the
launcher, the dock and Just Type: an Android device ships apps that can't be removed, and a
hidden app is simply left out. It keeps Palm's app id, so it sits where webOS users expect to
find it, and Palm's look and icons, so it belongs.

The app's code is Lunacy's, under the same terms as the rest of Lunacy. Its stylesheet
carries Palm's rules for the header and the app rows (from main/SWManager.css), marked there.
These files are not Lunacy's:

- icon.png, icon-256x256.png, images/swmanager_48x48.png

  Copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-Packard, from com.palm.app.swmanager 3.0.3400 as shipped on
  the reference TouchPad (webOS 3.0.5). Never released under an open licence; distributed by
  Lunacy as abandonware, like Mojo and the Prelude fonts (no owner has asserted rights since
  webOS was discontinued).
